  "caption": "Figure 2: Left. Language modeling (LM) ability for various NLP models, represented by crossentropy loss (lower is better) on the text corresponding to the Harry Potter dataset. We used 4- fold cross-validation. The booksum model has worse LM ability than the base model for BigBird and LED, but better for LongT5. It has no significant difference for BART. Hence, while all 4 booksum models have better brain alignment, most do not have better LM ability. This shows that the improved brain alignment in booksum models (shown in Figure 1) is due to deeper understanding, and not language modeling. Right. 20v20 accuracy is significantly higher for the model with deeper understanding (booksum) than LM model (base), across all brain language regions. This suggests that the function of deep understanding is not localized to any one particular region in the brain, and is instead distributed across language regions. Similar results were obtained for all other models (BART, LED, LongT5), shown in Appendix G. Overall, these results suggest the need to supplement training of NLP models beyond LM for improved language understanding.",
